.TH VECPS 1
.SH NAME
vecps \- draw vector files as pages of PostScript
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B vecps
[
.B \-w
.I x0 y0 x1 y1
|
.B \-r
.I x0 y0 x1 y1
|
.B \-p
.IR part [, part ...]
] ... [
.B \-n
]
.IR file [= r , g , b [, line ]]
\&...
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I Vecps
draws each
.IR vec (5)
file, the first underneath, in its color (black by default), filled
or, with
.BR line ,
as outlines, on a letter page, landscape; a first file with page
records (a sheet) is drawn as those pages, each at its size and scale
1, a page of PostScript for each: on page k, the records of each file
from its k-th page record to the next.
Text, and every name it writes, is drawn stroke by stroke in the stroke
font.
The window
.B \-w
is the region drawn, by default all the files, the layers of a board
whole (their drawing records, each line's width and each disk's radius
counted).
Clear polarity erases what its file drew before, as
.IR vec (5)
says, and nothing of the files under it: each run of a file's dark
records is drawn clipped off every clear record after it, so a layer's
silkscreen, cleared off the pads, leaves the copper under it showing.
On a sheet, each port of the first file links to pages, as
.IR schview (1)
follows a click on it: its circle and its name to the first page of its
list other than its own, each page number of its list but its own to
that page; the links are pdfmark annotations, each fitting its page in
the window and drawn with no border, which
.IR ps2pdf (1)
keeps; a global links nowhere, and a note is not printed.
.PP
A region render crops to a window and names what is in it, a sheet or a
board alike:
.B \-r
gives the window,
.B \-p
the parts, by name or designator (again, or with commas, for more),
whose boxes, grown by a fifth and 1 unit, make it.
Each part in the window shows its designator, from its part bracket, in
its box; each track and pad of a net, and each wire of a sheet, its
net's name, along the track or in the pad, sized to it but its capitals
no lower than 2 points on the page nor higher than 5, and a track too
short for its name goes without.
With
.B \-n
the names of the first file are written in their boxes.
It is the one program that makes pictures, of a board or a sheet;
.IR ps2pdf (1)
makes a PDF of them.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
schdraw ch1.sch > ch1.vec && vecps ch1.vec > ch1.ps && ps2pdf ch1.ps
vecps -w 86 -145 104 -115 theirs.vec=.7,.7,.7 ours.vec=.85,0,0,line > overlay.ps
cd vec && vecps -p R403,R404 top.vec=.8,.2,.2 topsilk.vec > term.ps
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
vec(5), gbrvec(1), ps2pdf(1)
